{
  "id": "COMPOUND:14268 - PROTEIN:2575",
  "verbalization": "Benzocaine is linked to Cyclin-dependent kinase 7 through a series of intermediate targets, all of which are modulated by 4-(3-Pyridin-2-Yl-1h-Pyrazol-4-Yl)Quinoline. This quinoline compound acts as a common mediator, with benzocaine directly targeting the quinoline, which in turn targets cyclin-dependent kinase 7. The evidence suggests that benzocaine may influence the activity of the quinoline, which then affects the kinase. This pathway implies a potential mechanism where benzocaine could modulate the quinoline's function, thereby influencing cyclin-dependent kinase 7 activity. The presence of multiple independent pathways linking benzocaine to the quinoline and ultimately to cyclin-dependent kinase 7 supports a consistent mechanism, though the exact nature of the interaction between benzocaine and the quinoline remains to be fully elucidated.",
